PWB xargs for Epoch68 UNIX V7
==============================

This is a focused ANSI C port of the historical PWB/UNIX xargs source
preserved in the archived UNIX768 repository's PWB source-intake tree. That
source came from
TUHS spencer_pwb.tar.gz, path sys/source/s2/xargs.c, with an archive timestamp
of 1980-02-10.

The command retains the historical option syntax and limits:

        -x          fail rather than split an oversized argument list
        -l          execute once per input line
        -i[pattern] substitute each input line for pattern (default {})
        -t          trace commands on standard error
        -e[string]  set the logical end-of-input string (default _)
        -s[number]  set maximum command-line size (maximum 470)
        -n[number]  use at most number input arguments per command
        -p          prompt on /dev/tty before executing

With no command, xargs runs /bin/echo.

The port replaces the missing PWB macros.h helpers, pre-V7 initialization and
assignment syntax, implicit pointer returns, ABI-dependent error-message
argument walking, and pexec() with typed V7 libc operations.  It intentionally
does not add modern GNU or POSIX extensions.
